    "seo_question": "What is the full narration of the story of Abraha and the Elephant from Shia hadith sources?",
    "summary": "This hadith from al-Amali of al-Shaykh al-Mufid narrates the famous story of the People of the Elephant (Ashab al-Fil), in which Abraha, the Abyssinian king, marched on Makkah to destroy the Ka'bah. Abdul Muttalib, the grandfather of the Prophet Muhammad (SAWW) and chief of Quraysh, confronted Abraha demanding only the return of his camels, declaring that the Ka'bah has its own Lord who will protect it. The story culminates in the miraculous divine intervention described in Surah al-Fil (105), where flocks of birds destroyed Abraha's army with stones, preserving the sanctity of the Sacred House.",
